\p
\v 1 King¦357738 Nevukadnetstsar¦357737 \add !(Nebuchadnezzar¦357737)\add* had a gold¦357743 statue¦357740 made¦357739 that stood nearly thirty metres high¦357744 and was almost three metres wide, and it¦357750 was erected on¦357751 the¦357751 Dura¦357752 plain¦357751 in¦357751 the¦357753 Babylonian province¦357753.
\v 2 Then¦357756 King¦357757 Nevukadnetstsar¦357776 sent¦357758 for the \add ≈various levels of\add* governors¦357763, the¦357764 counsellors¦357764, the¦357765 treasurers¦357765, the¦357766 judges¦357766, the¦357767 magistrates¦357767, and¦357756 all¦357768 the provincial¦357770 officials, to¦357771 all come¦357771 to¦357772 the¦357772 dedication¦357772 of¦357772 the¦357773 statue¦357773 that¦357774 \add *he'd¦357775\add* erected.
\v 3 \add ≈So all¦357788 those officials assembled¦357780 in¦357779 front¦357799 of¦357789 the statue that¦357793 the¦357796 king¦357796 had¦357794 set¦357794 up¦357794, ready\add* for¦357791 the¦357791 dedication¦357791.
\v 4 Then¦357805 the¦357805 herald¦357805 loudly proclaimed¦357806, “You¦357810 peoples¦357810, nations¦357811, and¦357812 languages¦357812 are¦357809 commanded
\v 5 that¦357815 any¦357826 time¦357814 you hear¦357817 the¦357818 sound¦357818 of¦357818 the¦357819 horn¦357819, flute¦357820, lyre, harps¦357824, pipes¦357825, and¦357826 \add ≈other instruments\add*, you all¦357826 must¦357817 bow down¦357829 and¦357830 worship¦357830 the gold¦357832 statue¦357831 that¦357833 King¦357836 Nevukadnetstsar¦357835 has¦357834 erected.
\v 6 \add ≈Anyone who refuses\add* to¦357849 bow down¦357843 and¦357844 worship¦357844 \add >it¦357845\add* at¦357845 that¦357840 time, will¦357843 be¦357848 thrown¦357848 into a blazing¦357853 furnace¦357851.”
\v 7 \add ≈So when all¦357864 those people¦357866 who had¦357887 gathered heard¦357863 the sounds¦357867 made by the musical¦357876 instruments\add*, they¦357883 all bowed down¦357877 to¦357884 worship¦357883 the gold¦357885 statue¦357884.
\s1 Daniel's three friends get tattled on
